# Ode to Joy, arranged by Claude and SZ. A string swell, then a walking bass under the tune; up a step at the end.
title: Ode to Joy
composer: Ludwig van Beethoven
arranger: Claude & SZ
about: The finale of Beethoven's Ninth Symphony (1824), which sets Friedrich Schiller's poem about joy and brotherhood. Beethoven was almost completely deaf when he wrote it. Today it is the anthem of Europe.
year: 1824
source: public-domain
category: classics
key: D major
hidden: true
style: orchestral
tempo: 112
time: 4/4

